{
  "_doc": "iOS visual QA scenes (docs/design/ios-visual-testing.md). nativeOnly (default: name starts with native-) = no -wgLocalMode, no driver. steps (tab | click | tag: give the first visible match a DOM id for a native tap | scroll: scroll that element's scroller to its end, until it is in the viewport | settingsPage | file: put a picked file, content text (default {}), on that <input type=file> | consent: open that TrialConsent sheet | firstrun: open the W1 first-run picker over the seeded vault, or W2 with \"trial\" | invite: open the F1 \"Have an invite?\" sheet | offer: InviteSheet.offer(that claim URL), the P3 route | inviteRequest: open the W5 \"Request an invite\" sheet with a stub POST, \"sent\" also sends it | openAccount: answer a placeholder shell base and open the W5 \"Open my account\" page with a full address, \"invalid\" commits a partial one) and ready (selectors that must be visible): the in-page driver (tests/visual/driver.js). native: XCUITest steps after #wg-qa-ready (ios/UITests): tap (DOM id or placeholder), type, clear, tapButton (label), waitFor (label or id), keyboard (wait for the software keyboard). Page scenes (Settings) open from Today first: a page keeps its origin tab lit, and each load restores the previous scene's tab, so without it Settings would light whatever ran before (med-e6ql). The page clock reads today 23:00 local (driver.js pinClock), so time-dependent text is stable. mask (optional): [{x, y, w, h}] fractions of the image that tests/visual/compare.mjs blanks before diffing (regions that still change run to run). localOnly: the cloud pass skips it. cloudOnly: the local passes (Playwright local, the iOS Simulator) skip it. platform (optional, \"ios\" or \"android\"): only that shell runs it. args (optional, native scenes): extra launch arguments, a `-key` here replacing the base one (Dynamic Type; the Debug-only -wgQALock failed|cancelled, -wgQALoadError 503|404|local, -wgQAHoldMark). settings-erase-confirm, settings-replace-confirm and settings-delete-confirm only open their typed-confirm dialogs (they never type the word); journey turns gamification ON for the device, so it stays last. startHere ({drop: vault data sections, picked: W1 picks}) replaces the seeded vault with a partial copy and reloads, so today-start-here runs after every other scene. trial (a trial status) stubs what the AI-trial offer reads (in account mode it also sets the trial flag the visual cloud server, with no trial key, leaves out). noAIKey answers the integrations read with the OpenAI key blank (the seed has one, which hides the Settings offer). localFeedback (true) answers App Attest and base.post for the page and mounts the local Settings → Send feedback row, scrolled into view (med-ta2n.20). kitNudge (a kit-nudge status) answers the Today kit card's status read with it, for the rest of the run.",
